## API only

This application was created with `forge new --api`. It serves JSON only:
`GET /` names the service, `GET /v1/status` is the example endpoint and Forge
adds `/health`, `/health/live` and `/health/ready`. Errors are JSON too. There
is no `app/views`, `app/assets`, `app/javascript` or `config/locales`, and
`app/bootstrap` installs no CSRF, method-override, flash or locale middleware:
authenticate API clients with a header (a bearer token), never a cookie.

The generators that write pages refuse this application: `forge generate
view`, `forge generate scaffold`, `forge generate authentication` and
`forge generate controller` without `--api`. `forge generate resource`,
`model`, `controller --api`, `mailer`, `job` and `migration` work as in a
full-stack application. For pages, create a full-stack application with
`forge new NAME` and move the code into it.
{{- else}}

## HTML pages

Server-rendered pages live in `app/views`: `layouts/application.gohtml`
wraps every page that defines a `content` block, partials are named
`_NAME.gohtml` (`shared/_flash.gohtml` shows flash messages), and the
stylesheet is `app/assets/application.css`. Build the renderer
once with `views.New(views.WithI18n(translator))` and render pages with
`RenderRequest`. `bootstrap.Configure` installs the locale negotiation,
method override (`_method` in forms), CSRF protection
(`{{"{{"}}csrfField{{"}}"}}` in every form) and flash messages for all
routes. See the Forge views guide (`docs/VIEWS.md`).

## Translations

User-visible text lives in `config/locales`: `en.json`{{if ne .Locale "en"}} and
`{{.Locale}}.json` (the default locale){{end}}, plus scoped files such as
`posts.en.json` that `forge generate scaffold` adds. Each file is one JSON
object whose only key is the locale; keys are dotted paths, `%{name}`
interpolates and `one`/`other` (CLDR plural forms) choose by `count`:

```json
{"pt-BR": {"posts": {"count": {"one": "%{count} post", "other": "%{count} posts"}}}}
```

Pages use `{{"{{"}}t "posts.index.title"{{"}}"}}`,
`{{"{{"}}t "posts.count" "count" .Total{{"}}"}}`, `{{"{{"}}l .CreatedAt "short"{{"}}"}}` and
`{{"{{"}}number .Price 2{{"}}"}}`; Go code uses `i18n.T(r.Context(), "posts.flash.created")`.
Each request gets the locale of the `locale` cookie, then `Accept-Language`,
then the default (`FORGE_I18N_DEFAULT_LOCALE`, else `{{.Locale}}`).

```bash
cp config/locales/en.json config/locales/fr.json   # then translate it and rename the top-level key to "fr"
forge i18n check                                   # keys each locale lacks, plural forms, unused keys
curl -H 'Accept-Language: {{.Locale}}' http://127.0.0.1:8080/
FORGE_I18N_DEFAULT_LOCALE=en forge dev             # serve English by default
```

Missing translations show as `translation missing: LOCALE.KEY` in
development and test and fall back to the default locale in production. See
the Forge i18n guide (`docs/I18N.md`).

## JavaScript and styles
{{if .JS}}
There is no Node toolchain. Static files are embedded in the binary and
served with content-digested names (`/assets/application-<digest>.css`) and
immutable caching; Turbo and Stimulus are vendored by Forge and loaded
through an import map (no inline scripts: the page policy allows the map by
hash).

| Path | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| `app/assets/` | stylesheet and images (add the file name to the `go:embed` line in `assets.go`) |
| `app/javascript/application.js` | entry point: `import "@hotwired/turbo"` and `import "controllers"` |
| `app/javascript/controllers/` | Stimulus controllers, one `NAME_controller.js` each, registered in `index.js` |

Add a Stimulus controller:

```bash
cp app/javascript/controllers/hello_controller.js app/javascript/controllers/clipboard_controller.js
# then add to app/javascript/controllers/index.js:
#   import ClipboardController from "controllers/clipboard_controller"
#   application.register("clipboard", ClipboardController)
```

and use it in a template with `data-controller="clipboard"`. Files in
`controllers/` are embedded and pinned automatically; rebuild (`forge dev`
does) to serve a change under its new digested URL. Real-time updates:
`forge generate scaffold NAME ... --broadcast` (see `docs/VIEWS.md`).
{{- else}}
The front end is TypeScript. There is no Node toolchain and no bundler:
`forge dev`, `forge build`, `forge test` and `forge check` strip the types
with esbuild (built into `forge`) and write plain JavaScript to
`app/javascript/dist`, which the binary embeds. Static files are embedded in
the binary and served with content-digested names
(`/assets/application-<digest>.css`) and immutable caching; Turbo and Stimulus
are vendored by Forge and loaded through an import map (no inline scripts: the
page policy allows the map by hash).

| Path | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| `app/assets/` | stylesheet and images (add the file name to the `go:embed` line in `assets.go`) |
| `app/javascript/application.ts` | entry point: `import "@hotwired/turbo"` and `import "controllers"` |
| `app/javascript/controllers/` | Stimulus controllers, one `NAME_controller.ts` each, registered in `index.ts` |
| `app/javascript/dist/` | the compiled JavaScript the binary embeds: generated, committed, never edited |
| `app/javascript/types/` | declarations of Turbo and Stimulus for `tsc`, copied unchanged from npm |
| `tsconfig.json` | strict `tsc --noEmit` settings; the import map's bare names are `paths` |

```bash
forge dev      # recompiles on every change to a .ts file (inline source maps)
forge build    # compiles app/javascript to dist, then builds bin/{{.Name}}
forge check    # also runs tsc --noEmit when tsc is on PATH
```

esbuild only strips types; `tsc` checks them. Install it once with
`npm install --global --ignore-scripts typescript@{{.TypeScriptVersion}}` (Node is needed for
that and nothing else); without it `forge check` prints one note and skips the
type check. The generated CI installs the same pinned version and runs
`tsc --noEmit`, and `go test` fails when a `.ts` file changed and `dist` did
not, or when a compiled file is not the one `forge` wrote, so run `forge build`
(or `forge test`) before you commit, and review `dist/` diffs like code. A `.ts`
file outside `controllers/` is compiled and embedded too; pin it in
`app/assets/assets.go` (`forgeassets.PinAllFrom(set, "lib")`) to import it by name.

Add a Stimulus controller:

```bash
cp app/javascript/controllers/hello_controller.ts app/javascript/controllers/clipboard_controller.ts
# then add to app/javascript/controllers/index.ts:
#   import ClipboardController from "controllers/clipboard_controller"
#   application.register("clipboard", ClipboardController)
forge build    # or let forge dev do it
```

and use it in a template with `data-controller="clipboard"`. Files in
`controllers/` are compiled, embedded and pinned automatically. Real-time
updates: `forge generate scaffold NAME ... --broadcast` (see `docs/VIEWS.md`).
To keep plain JavaScript instead, create the application with `forge new --js`.
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
